{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\ntypedef long long llong;\nconst llong MOD = 1000000007LL;\n\nllong computePower(llong base, llong exponent, llong modulus) {\n    llong result = 1;\n    for (llong i = 0; i < exponent; ++i) {\n        result = (result * base) % modulus;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nllong computeModPower(llong base, llong exponent) {\n    return computePower(base, exponent, MOD);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    llong p, k;\n    cin >> p >> k;\n    \n    llong remainder = k % p;\n    if (remainder == 1) {\n        cout << computeModPower(p, p);\n        return 0;\n    }\n    \n    if (remainder == 0) {\n        cout << computeModPower(p, p - 1);\n        return 0;\n    }\n    \n    llong order = 1;\n    while (true) {\n        if ((p - 1) % order != 0) {\n            ++order;\n            continue;\n        }\n        if (computePower(k, order, p) == 1) {\n            break;\n        }\n        ++order;\n    }\n    \n    cout << computeModPower(p, (p - 1) / order);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\ndef compute_power(base, exponent, modulus):\n    result = 1\n    for _ in range(exponent):\n        result = (result * base) % modulus\n    return result\n\ndef compute_mod_power(base, exponent):\n    MOD = 1000000007\n    return compute_power(base, exponent, MOD)\n\ndef main():\n    p, k = map(int, input().split())\n    \n    remainder = k % p\n    if remainder == 1:\n        print(compute_mod_power(p, p))\n        return\n    \n    if remainder == 0:\n        print(compute_mod_power(p, p - 1))\n        return\n    \n    order = 1\n    while True:\n        if (p - 1) % order != 0:\n            order += 1\n            continue\n        if compute_power(k, order, p) == 1:\n            break\n        order += 1\n    \n    print(compute_mod_power(p, (p - 1) // order))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00012730741582345217, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.5402160286903381, -0.0006224363460205495, -0.012558897957205772, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -3.933898824470816e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -1.0251946150674485e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.029752036556601524, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.684815212385729e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.529942543740617e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -3.6954811548639555e-06, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -0.0052368370816111565, -6.151010165922344e-05, -4.768360213347478e-06, -6.556489552167477e-06, -1.5497195136049413e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.4437606043647975e-05, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.008629176765680313, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389